\p
\v 1 Then¦202445 Shelomoh¦202447 \add !(Solomon¦202447)\add* \add ≈prayed\add*, “\add ≈Yahweh¦202448, you said¦202449 that you\add* would live¦202450 in¦202451 a \add ≈dark¦202451\add* cloud,
\v 2 \add ≈but¦202453\add* I've¦202454 built¦202454 a¦202455 \add ≈beautiful\add* residence for¦202458 you¦202458—a¦202459 place¦202459 for you¦202460 to¦202460 live¦202460 in¦202460 forever¦202461.”
\p
\v 3 ⇔\add ≈Then, while all the people stood¦202478\add* \add there\add*, Shelomoh turned¦202463 toward them and¦202468 \add ≈spoke a blessing¦202468 over\add* them,
\v 4 saying¦202480, “Yahweh¦202482, Yisrael's¦202484 \add !(Israel¦202484)\add* god¦202483, is¦202481 blessed¦202481, who¦202485 spoke¦202486 \add ≈physically\add* to my¦202490 father¦202490 David¦202489, and¦202491 \add ≈then caused it to actually happen\add*, when he said¦202493 \add back then\add*,\x + \xo 6:4-9: \xt 2Sam 7:1-13; 1Ch 17:1-12.\x*
\v 5 ‘When¦202498 I¦202499 brought¦202499 my people out¦202499 of Mitsrayim¦202504 \add !(Egypt¦202504)\add*, I¦202507 hadn't chosen¦202507 a¦202508 city¦202508 from¦202509 all¦202509 of¦202510 Yisrael's¦202511 tribes¦202510 as a place to¦202512 build¦202512 a¦202513 house¦202513 so¦202517 my¦202515 name¦202515 could be there¦202516. Nor had I¦202519 chosen¦202519 a¦202520 man¦202520 to¦202521 be¦202521 leader¦202522 over¦202523 my people, Yisrael¦202526,
\v 6 \add ≈but¦202528\add* \add now\add* I've¦202528 chosen¦202528 Yerushalem¦202529 \add !(Jerusalem¦202529)\add* \add ≈to¦202530 be¦202530 my place of residence\add*, and¦202533 I've¦202533 chosen¦202533 \add you\add*, David¦202534, to¦202535 be¦202535 over¦202536 my¦202538 people¦202538, Yisrael¦202539.’
\p
\v 7 “My¦202546 father¦202546 David¦202545 wanted to¦202547 build¦202547 a¦202548 temple¦202548 for¦202549 Yisrael's¦202552 god¦202551 Yahweh¦202550,
\v 8 \add ≈but¦202554\add* Yahweh¦202555 told¦202554 \add *him¦202558\add*, ‘\add ≈It's good that¦202561 you wanted to¦202566 build¦202566 a¦202567 house¦202567 to honour me\add*,
\v 9 \add ≈but\add* you¦202577 won't¦202578 be the one to build it. It'll be your own \add ≈biological\add* son¦202582 who'll¦202583 build¦202587 the¦202588 temple¦202588 to honour my¦202589 \add ≈reputation¦202589\add*.’
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈Now\add* Yahweh¦202592 has¦202591 fulfilled what he¦202597 said¦202597, and I'm here sitting¦202602 on¦202604 Yisrael's throne¦202606 instead of¦202606 my¦202601 father¦202601 David¦202600, just¦202608 as¦202608 Yahweh¦202610 said¦202609, and¦202611 I've¦202611 had¦202611 this temple¦202612 built¦202611 to honour Yisrael's god¦202615 Yahweh.
\v 11 I've¦202618 placed¦202618 the¦202622 \add sacred\add* box¦202622 in there¦202625—\add @the box\add* that¦202628 contains the¦202626 agreement¦202626 Yahweh¦202627 made¦202629 with¦202630 Yisrael's¦202633 descendants.”
\s1 Shelomoh's prayer
\rem /s1 Solomon's Prayer; Solomon's Prayer of Dedication
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 8:22-53)
\p
\v 12 Then¦202635 \add @Shelomoh¦202635\add* \add !(Solomon¦202635)\add* stood¦202635 in¦202636 front¦202636 of¦202636 the¦202637 altar¦202637 to Yahweh¦202638 in¦202639 front¦202639 of¦202639 all¦202640 the¦202642 assembled¦202642 Israelis¦202643, and¦202644 spread¦202644 out¦202644 his¦202645 hands¦202645,
\v 13 because¦202647 \add *he'd¦202650\add* made¦202649 a¦202651 bronze¦202652 platform and¦202653 had¦202653 it¦202653 placed¦202653 in¦202654 the¦202654 centre¦202654 of¦202655 the¦202655 courtyard¦202655. The square platform was just over two metres on each side, and stood just over a metre off the ground. \add ≈Firstly\add* he¦202665 stood¦202665 on¦202666 it¦202666, then¦202667 he¦202667 knelt¦202667 down¦202667 \add ≈in¦202671 front¦202671 of¦202671\add* all¦202672 the¦202674 assembled¦202674 Israelis¦202675 and¦202676 spread¦202676 his hands¦202677 out¦202676 to¦202678 the¦202678 \add #sky¦202678\add*
\v 14 and¦202680 said¦202680, “Yahweh¦202681, Yisrael's¦202683 \add !(Israel¦202683)\add* god, there¦202684 isn't¦202684 any god like¦202686 you¦202686 in¦202688 the heavens¦202688 or on¦202689 the earth¦202689—one who¦202690 keeps¦202690 \add &his¦202691\add* agreement¦202691 and¦202692 \add shows\add* loyal¦202692 commitment¦202692 to¦202693 your¦202693 servants¦202693 who¦202694 are walking¦202694 \add ≈with total¦202696 integrity as you watch them\add*.
\v 15 \add ≈Everything you¦202701 verbally told my father¦202704 David¦202703 that¦202706 you'd do, you've¦202713 used your power to¦202709 make it¦202709 all happen, including this¦202715 today\add*.
\v 16 And¦202717 now¦202717, Yahweh¦202718, Yisrael's¦202721 god¦202720, keep¦202722 \add another promise you made\add* to¦202723 your¦202723 servant¦202723 David¦202725 my¦202726 father¦202726, when you¦202729 told¦202729 him¦202730, ‘There'll \add ≈always be¦202734 one¦202736 of¦202737 your descendants¦202747 sitting¦202738 on¦202739 Yisrael's¦202742 throne¦202741, as long as they¦202746 obey my¦202752 instructions¦202752 just¦202753 like¦202753 you¦202754 have¦202754\add*.’\x + \xo 6:16: \xt 1Ki 2:4.\x*
\v 17 \add ≈So¦202757\add* now¦202757, Yahweh¦202758, Yisrael's¦202760 god¦202759, may what you¦202764 said¦202764 to¦202765 your¦202765 servant¦202765, to¦202766 David¦202766, be¦202761 confirmed.
\p
\v 18 “But will¦202770 God¦202771 really¦202769 live¦202770 with¦202772 humans¦202774 \add here\add* on¦202775 the¦202777 earth¦202777? Wow, the skies¦202779 and¦202780 the¦202780 heavens¦202780 of¦202780 the¦202781 heavens¦202781 can't¦202782 contain¦202783 you¦202783—how much less this¦202788 house¦202787 that¦202789 I've¦202790 built¦202790.\x + \xo 6:18: \xt 2Ch 2:6.\x*
\v 19 \add ≈Nevertheless\add* Yahweh¦202800 my¦202801 god¦202801, listen¦202802 to¦202803 your servant's prayer¦202811 and request \add ≈and take notice\add*.
\v 20 \add ≈Watch over this¦202820 building\add* where¦202826 you¦202827 said¦202827 \add ≈you'd be present\add*,\x + \xo 6:20: \xt Deu 12:11.\x* and hear¦202831 \add &my¦202834\add* \add #prayers¦202834\add* when your¦202837 servant¦202837 prays¦202836 towards this place.
\v 21 Listen¦202843 \add ≈to¦202844 what your¦202847 servant¦202847 and¦202848 your¦202848 Israeli¦202849 people¦202848 are requesting\add* when they¦202851 pray¦202851 towards this¦202855 place. Listen¦202857 from¦202858 where you live¦202859 in the¦202862 heavens¦202862, and¦202863 hear¦202863 and¦202864 forgive¦202864.
\p
\v 22 “If¦202866 someone¦202869 \add is accused of\add* wronging their neighbour¦202870, and is forced to make a sworn statement in¦202878 front¦202878 of¦202878 your¦202879 altar¦202879 in¦202880 this¦202881 temple¦202880,
\v 23 then¦202883 \add ≈listen¦202885\add* from¦202886 the¦202888 heavens¦202888 and¦202889 \add ≈decide who's telling the truth\add*. \add ≈Then¦202890 punish the guilty¦202895 party as they deserve, and¦202899 do good to¦202899 the other side as a¦202900 reward¦202894 for their innocence\add*.
\p
\v 24 “And¦202906 if¦202906 your Israeli¦202910 people¦202909 are¦202908 \add ≈defeated¦202908 by their enemies¦202912 because¦202913 they've¦202914 disobeyed\add* you¦202916, but¦202917 they¦202917 return¦202917 \add to you\add* and¦202918 confess, and¦202922 pray¦202922, and¦202923 in¦202925 this¦202926 place they¦202923 \add ≈request¦202923 your\add* favour¦202923,
\v 25 then¦202928 listen¦202929 to them from¦202930 the¦202932 heavens¦202932 and¦202933 forgive¦202933 your¦202935 Israeli¦202936 people's¦202935 disobedience, and¦202937 bring¦202937 them¦202937 back¦202937 to¦202938 this land¦202940 that¦202941 you¦202943 gave¦202943 to¦202944 their¦202945 ancestors¦202945 and¦202945 to¦202945 them.
\p
\v 26 “When¦202948 \add ≈the¦202949 clouds hold back¦202968\add* and¦202950 give no rain¦202953 because¦202954 \add ≈your Israeli people have disobeyed\add* you¦202957, but then they¦202958 pray¦202958 towards this¦202962 place¦202961 and \add ≈acknowledge you\add* and turn¦202968 away from¦202967 their¦202967 disobedience because¦202969 you've¦202970 punished them¦202970,
\v 27 then¦202972 listen¦202974 to them from the¦202975 heavens¦202975 and¦202976 forgive¦202976 the¦202977 \add ≈disobedience\add* of¦202977 your¦202978 servants¦202978 and¦202979 your¦202979 Israeli¦202980 people. Teach them¦202982 the¦202985 \add ≈right¦202986 way¦202985 to live their lives\add*, and¦202991 give¦202991 rain¦202992 to your¦202995 land¦202995 which¦202996 you¦202998 gave¦202998 your people as a \add ≈permanent inheritance¦203000\add*.
\p
\v 28 “If¦203004 this land¦203007 \add suffers\add* from famine¦203003, or if¦203009 there's blight¦203012 or mildew¦203013, or locusts or grasshoppers, \add ≈deadly diseases¦203027\add* or sickness¦203030, or if an enemy¦203022 \add army\add* surrounds them,
\v 29 then if any¦203040 person¦203042, or all¦203043 your¦203044 Israeli¦203045 people¦203044, stretch¦203051 out¦203051 their hands¦203052 towards this¦203056 temple¦203055 with their \add #prayers¦203034\add* and¦203043 requests because¦203043 they¦203047 each acknowledge¦203047 their individual pain¦203050 and¦203051 suffering,
\v 30 then¦203058 listen¦203059 to them from¦203060 where you live¦203064 there in the¦203062 heavens¦203062, and¦203065 forgive¦203065 them. \add ≈Reward\add* each¦203068 person¦203067 according¦203068 to¦203068 their behaviour¦203070, because¦203076 you know \add ≈people's motives\add*—only you know¦203079 \add ≈what's in people's minds¦203082\add*.
\v 31 \add Do that\add* so¦203086 they'll¦203087 respect¦203087 you and \add ≈live how you want them to¦203088\add*, as they¦203095 live¦203096 in \add ≈this country\add* that¦203101 you¦203102 gave¦203102 to¦203103 our¦203103 ancestors¦203103.
\p
\v 32 “Also¦203106, any foreigners¦203109 who¦203110 don't¦203111 belong to your¦203112 Israeli¦203113 people¦203112, who come¦203115 to this land¦203117 because¦203119 they've \add ≈heard that you're very great¦203121 and¦203122 powerful¦203123\add*, if they¦203126 turn toward this temple¦203130 and¦203127 pray¦203127,
\v 33 then¦203133 listen¦203134 to them \add as well\add* from¦203135 where you live¦203139 there in the¦203137 heavens¦203137. Do¦203140 whatever that¦203142 foreigner¦203146 requests from you, so¦203147 that¦203147 all¦203149 the¦203151 people¦203151 groups in the¦203152 world¦203152 will learn¦203148 about your¦203155 \add ≈reputation¦203155\add*, and¦203156 \add ≈honour¦203156 and obey\add* you¦203157 like¦203158 your¦203158 Israeli¦203159 people do, and¦203160 know¦203160 that¦203161 this¦203168 temple¦203167 that¦203169 I've¦203170 built¦203170 is¦203164 called¦203164 by your name.
\p
\v 34 “When you¦203182 send¦203182 your¦203175 people¦203175 off to battle¦203176 their enemies¦203179, and¦203183 they¦203183 pray¦203183 towards this city¦203186 that¦203188 you've¦203189 chosen¦203189 and¦203191 this temple¦203191 that¦203192 I've¦203194 had¦203194 built¦203194 \add to honour\add* your¦203195 name¦203195,
\v 35 then¦203197 listen¦203197 from¦203198 the¦203200 heavens¦203200 to their¦203203 prayer¦203203 and¦203204 their¦203206 requests, and¦203207 \add ≈uphold their¦203208 cause¦203207\add*.
\p
\v 36 “When they¦203211 disobey you¦203213 (and there's¦203215 no one who¦203217 doesn't), and¦203221 you're¦203221 angry¦203221 with¦203222 them¦203222 and¦203223 allow an¦203225 enemy¦203225 \add ≈to get the upper hand¦203223\add*, and¦203226 their¦203227 captors¦203227 take¦203226 them¦203226 to¦203228 a¦203230 distant¦203231 or¦203232 nearby¦203233 land¦203230 as captives¦203226,
\v 37 and¦203235 then in that land¦203239 where¦203240 they're¦203241 \add ≈captives¦203241\add*, they¦203244 turn and¦203246 admit their¦203249 wickedness and their¦203249 disobedience, and¦203253 request¦203246 your favour¦203246,
\v 38 and¦203255 they¦203255 turn¦203255 to¦203256 you¦203256 with total sincerity in¦203263 that other country¦203263, and¦203269 pray¦203269 towards the¦203270 land¦203271 that¦203272 you¦203273 gave¦203273 their¦203274 ancestors¦203274, and¦203275 the¦203275 city¦203275 that¦203276 you¦203277 chose¦203277, and¦203278 toward the temple¦203278 that¦203279 I've¦203281 built¦203281 \add to honour\add* your¦203282 name¦203282,
\v 39 then¦203284 listen¦203284 from¦203286 where you live¦203290 in the¦203288 heavens¦203288 to their¦203293 prayer¦203293 and¦203294 their¦203296 requests, and¦203297 \add ≈uphold their¦203298 cause¦203297\add* and¦203299 forgive¦203299 your¦203300 people¦203300 who've \add ≈disobeyed¦203302\add* you¦203304.
\p
\v 40 “Now¦203306 my¦203307 god¦203307, please¦203310 let¦203308 your¦203311 eyes¦203311 be open¦203312 and¦203313 your¦203313 ears¦203313 attentive¦203314 to¦203315 \add #prayers¦203315\add* \add offered towards\add* this¦203317 place¦203316.
\p
\v 41 “\add ≈So¦203320\add* now¦203320 Yahweh¦203322 God¦203323, along with the¦203326 \add sacred\add* box¦203326 \add ≈representing\add* your¦203327 strength¦203327, come and enter your place¦203324 for resting¦203324. Yahweh¦203329 God¦203330, may your¦203328 priests¦203328 be¦203331 dressed¦203331 in \add your\add* rescue¦203332, and¦203333 your¦203333 faithful¦203333 \add >ones\add* enjoy \add your\add* goodness¦203335.\x + \xo 6:41-42: \xt Psa 132:8-10.\x*
\v 42 Yahweh¦203337 God¦203338, don't¦203339 \add ≈ignore\add* those who you've chosen. Remember¦203344 your¦203347 servant¦203347 David's¦203346 loyal¦203345 commitment¦203345.”
\c 7
