\v 21 because¦204601 the¦204604 king's¦204604 ships went¦204605 to Tarshish¦204606 with¦204607 Huram's¦204609 servants¦204608. Every three¦204611 years¦204612 the¦204615 fleet would \add ≈bring¦204617 back\add* gold¦204618, silver¦204619, ivory¦204620, and¦204621 apes and¦204622 baboons,
\v 22 \add ≈so¦204625\add* King¦204626 Shelomoh¦204627 \add became\add* greater¦204625 than¦204628 all¦204628 the¦204629 other kings¦204629 in the¦204630 world¦204630, \add both\add* in wealth¦204631 and¦204632 in wisdom¦204632.
\p
\v 23 \add ≈Kings¦204635 from all¦204634 over the¦204636 world¦204636 wanted¦204637 to¦204642 come and listen¦204642\add* to the wisdom¦204645 that¦204646 God had¦204648 \add ≈given\add* Shelomoh¦204641.
\v 24 Each¦204654 of them would bring¦204653 gifts: gold¦204659 and silver¦204657 items¦204658, clothes¦204660, myrrh and¦204662 spices¦204662, horses¦204663 and¦204664 mules¦204664. (\add This continued\add* \add ≈year¦204667 after year¦204668\add*.)
\p
\v 25 Shelomoh¦204672 had four¦204673 thousand¦204674 stalls¦204675 for horses¦204676 and¦204677 chariots¦204677, and¦204678 twelve thousand¦204681 horsemen¦204682, and¦204683 he¦204683 kept \add some\add* in¦204684 the¦204684 chariot cities¦204684 and¦204686 \add some\add* \add ≈close by\add* in¦204689 Yerushalem¦204689 \add !(Jerusalem¦204689)\add*.\x + \xo 9:25: \xt 1Ki 4:26.\x*
\v 26 He¦204691 \add ended up\add* ruling¦204692 over all¦204693 the¦204695 kings¦204695 \add in the region\add*, from¦204696 the¦204698 \add Perat\add* \add !(Euphrates)\add* River¦204698 \add in the northeast\add*, \add west\add* to¦204699 the¦204701 area of¦204701 the¦204702 Pelishtim¦204702, and¦204703 \add south down\add* to¦204703 the¦204704 Mitsri¦204705 \add !(Egyptian¦204705)\add* border¦204704.\x + \xo 9:26: \xt Gen 15:18; 1Ki 4:21.\x*
\v 27 The¦204708 king¦204708 made¦204716 silver¦204711 \add as common\add* as¦204713 stones¦204713, and¦204714 cedar¦204715 \add timber as common\add* as¦204717 the sycamore¦204717 fig trees in the lowlands.
\v 28 Horses¦204724 were¦204723 brought¦204723 in from¦204725 Mitsrayim¦204725 \add !(Egypt¦204725)\add*\x + \xo 9:28: \xt Deu 17:16.\x* for¦204726 Shelomoh¦204726, and¦204727 from¦204727 \add ≈other countries¦204729 as well\add*.
\s1 Summary of Shelomoh's reign
\rem /s1 Summary of Solomon's Reign; Death of Solomon; Solomon's Death
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 11:41-43)
\p
\v 29 Everything else that Shelomoh¦204733 \add !(Solomon¦204733)\add* did, from the¦204734 beginning to the¦204735 end, was¦204738 written¦204739 down by the¦204742 prophet Natan¦204743 \add !(Nathan¦204743)\add*, and¦204745 in the¦204747 prophecy¦204747 by Ahiyah¦204748 (from Shiloh), and¦204750 the¦204750 prophet Ido's¦204751 visions¦204750 about¦204757 Nevat's¦204759 son¦204757 Yarov'am¦204756 \add !(Jeroboam¦204756)\add* \add ≡were also written down\add*.
\v 30 Shelomoh¦204762 reigned¦204761 from Yerushalem¦204763 \add !(Jerusalem¦204763)\add* over¦204764 all¦204766 of¦204766 Yisrael¦204768 \add !(Israel¦204768)\add* for forty¦204769 years¦204770,
\v 31 then¦204772 \add *he¦204773\add* \add ≈died\add* and¦204777 was buried¦204777 with his¦204780 father¦204780 in¦204778 ‘The¦204778 City¦204778 of¦204778 David¦204779’, and¦204781 his¦204783 son¦204783 Rehav'am¦204782 \add !(Rehoboam¦204782)\add* \add ≈replaced him¦204784 as king¦204781\add*.
\c 10
\s1 Yisrael splits in two
\rem /s1 Kings of Judah; The Revolt against Rehoboam; Israel Rebels Against Rehoboam; The Northern Tribes Revolt
\s4 Full kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 12:1-20)
\p
\v 1 Then¦204787 Rehav'am¦204788 \add !(Rehoboam¦204788)\add* went¦204787 to¦204789 Shekem¦204789, \add *where¦204791\add* all¦204793 of¦204793 Yisrael¦204795 \add !(Israel¦204795)\add* had¦204792 gathered \add ≈for his coronation\add*.
\v 2 \add ≈Meanwhile\add*, Nevat's¦204804 son¦204802 Yarov'am \add !(Jeroboam)\add* had¦204808 fled¦204808 from¦204809 King¦204811 Shelomoh¦204810 \add !(Solomon¦204810)\add* and was \add down\add* in Mitsrayim \add !(Egypt)\add*, \add ≈but\add* when he heard¦204800 \add about the coming coronation\add*, \add *he\add* returned¦204812 from¦204814 Mitsrayim¦204814.
\v 3 \add ≈So\add* the leaders of the northern tribes summoned¦204817 \add @Yarov'am¦204819\add*, and¦204820 \add *he¦204821\add* went¦204820 with them to speak¦204825 to¦204826 \add Shelomoh's son\add* Rehav'am¦204828 and¦204822 all¦204822 of Yisrael¦204824, saying¦204829,
\v 4 “Your father \add ≈made¦204832 us work¦204838 very hard¦204832, but¦204836\add* now¦204836, lighten¦204837 the \add ≈demands that¦204843\add* your¦204839 father¦204839 \add ≈made on¦204846\add* us¦204846, and¦204847 we'll¦204847 serve¦204847 you¦204847.”
\p
\v 5 “Come back to¦204850 me in three¦204852 days¦204853.” \add @Rehav'am¦204855\add* \add ≈answered¦204849\add*, so¦204856 the¦204857 people¦204857 departed¦204856.
\p
\v 6 Then¦204860 King¦204861 Rehav'am¦204862 consulted¦204860 with¦204863 the¦204865 older¦204865 men¦204865 who'd¦204866 advised his¦204872 father¦204872 Shelomoh¦204871 when¦204873 he was¦204873 \add still\add* alive¦204874, \add ≈asking¦204875\add* \add &them\add*, “How¦204876 do you¦204877 advise¦204878 me to answer the people¦204880?”
\p
\v 7 “If¦204888 you're¦204890 good¦204891 to¦204892 those people¦204892 and¦204894 \add ≈do things that¦204893 please them¦204894\add*, and¦204895 speak¦204895 \add ≈kindly\add* to¦204896 them¦204896,” they \add ≈answered\add*, “then¦204899 they'll¦204899 \add ≈serve you for¦204900 a long time¦204904 to come\add*.”
\p
\v 8 \add ≈However,\add* \add @Rehav'am¦204906\add* \add ≈rejected¦204906 their advice¦204909\add*, and¦204913 consulted¦204913 some of the¦204916 young¦204916 men \add ≈there\add* who'd¦204917 grown¦204918 up¦204918 with¦204919 him.
\v 9 “\add ≈How would you¦204926 guys suggest I answer the¦204932 people¦204932 who've asked me¦204936 to¦204937 lighten¦204938 the¦204941 burden on them, compared to my father's¦204945 time\add*?”
\p
\v 10 “\add ≈Those people¦204958 tell you¦204957 that¦204959 your father was hard¦204965 on them and¦204969 that you¦204969 should lighten¦204970 their load\add*,” \add ≈his contemporaries advised him\add*. “\add ≈But you¦204973 should tell¦204973 them¦204974 that your little¦204975 finger¦204975 is¦204976 thicker¦204976 than¦204977 your father's¦204978 waist¦204977\add*,
\v 11 \add ≈and¦204980 that whereas he¦204982 required them to¦204988 contribute, you'll be even more demanding. Tell them that he¦204992 might\add* have whipped \add %them¦204993\add* with¦204994 \add leather\add* whips¦204994, but¦204995 that \add %you'll\add* whip \add %them\add* with¦204996 scorpions¦204996!”
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So¦204999\add* Yarov'am¦205000 \add !(Jeroboam¦205000)\add* and¦205001 all¦205001 the¦205003 people¦205003 \add ≈returned¦205013\add* to¦205004 \add King\add* Rehav'am¦205006 on the third day \add ≈as¦205009 he'd¦205010 prearranged\add*,
\v 13 and¦205021 ignoring the advice¦205025 of¦205025 the¦205026 older¦205026 men¦205026, the king answered¦205018 \add @the people\add* harshly.
\v 14 \add ≈He¦205028 passed on the¦205030 younger men's suggestion\add*, telling \add &the¦205031 people¦205031\add*, “I'll¦205033 make¦205033 your¦205036 \add ≈burden even heavier\add*. My¦205040 father¦205040 rebuked you¦205042 \add people\add* with¦205043 whips¦205043, but¦205044 I'll¦205044 \add ≡do it\add* with¦205045 scorpions¦205045.”
\v 15 \add ≈So¦205047\add* the¦205050 king¦205050 \add ≈took no notice of the¦205053 people's¦205053 request\add*, because¦205054 \add ≈it¦205056 was¦205056 God turning¦205057 events around, so¦205060 that¦205066 what Yahweh¦205062 had¦205067 said¦205067 to¦205071 Yarov'am¦205073 (Nevat's¦205076 son¦205074) through Ahiyah¦205069 (from Shiloh) would come to pass\add*.
\p
\v 16 \add ≈When¦205078\add* all¦205078 \add ≈the Israelis¦205080\add* saw that the¦205085 king¦205085 hadn't listened¦205084 to¦205086 them¦205086, the¦205088 people¦205088 \add from the northern tribes\add* answered the¦205091 king¦205091, “What¦205094 \add ≈did David¦205098 have to do with us anyway\add*? \add ≈We had nothing to gain\add* from Yishay's¦205104 \add !(Jesse¦205104)\add* son¦205102. \add ≈You might as well all head home, and then they'll see what happened to¦205106 David's¦205111 dynasty\add*.”\x + \xo 10:16: \xt 2Sam 20:1.\x*
\p \add ≈So¦205112 they all¦205113 went¦205112 home¦205116\add*,
\v 17 and¦205119 Rehav'am¦205126 \add ended up\add* \add ≈only ruling¦205124 over¦205125 the¦205119 Israelis¦205120 living¦205121 in¦205122 the¦205122 Yehudah¦205123\add* \add !(Judah¦205123)\add* \add ≈region\add*.
\p
\v 18 King¦205129 Rehav'am¦205130 \add (still in Shekem)\add* sent¦205128 out Hadoram¦205133, his supervisor of the¦205137 forced¦205137 labourers¦205137, but¦205138 the¦205141 \add ≈Israelis¦205143 hurled stones¦205144 at him and killed¦205138 him¦205140\add*. \add When he heard about that\add*, King¦205146 Rehav'am¦205147 \add ≈forced his way into his\add* chariot¦205150 \add ≈and escaped\add* to¦205151 Yerushalem¦205152 \add !(Jerusalem¦205152)\add*,
\v 19 and¦205155 \add northern\add* Yisrael¦205156 \add !(Israel¦205156)\add* has¦205155 rebelled¦205155 against David's¦205158 \add ≈descendants\add* to this¦205161 day¦205160.
\c 11
\s1 The scolding of prophet Simayass to Rehav'am
\rem /s1 Judah and Benjamin Fortified; Shemaiah's Prophecy
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 12:21-24)
\p
\v 1 When¦205164 Rehav'am¦205165 \add !(Rehoboam¦205165)\add* \add ≈arrived¦205164 in\add* Yerushalem¦205166 \add !(Jerusalem¦205166)\add*, he¦205167 assembled¦205167 Yehudah's¦205171 \add !(Judah¦205171)\add* and¦205172 Benyamin's¦205172 \add ≈warriors\add*: 180,000 chosen¦205176 to¦205179 fight¦205179 against Yisrael¦205182 \add !(Israel¦205182)\add* to¦205183 bring the¦205186 kingdom¦205186 back to¦205187 Rehav'am¦205187.
\v 2 \add ≈But¦205190\add* Yahweh¦205193 \add ≈spoke\add* to¦205194 the prophet Shemayah¦205196, saying¦205200,
\v 3 “\add Go and\add* tell¦205202 \add ≈this\add* to¦205203 Shelomoh's¦205208 \add !(Solomon¦205208)\add* son¦205206 King¦205209 Rehav'am¦205205 of¦205209 Yehudah¦205210, and¦205211 to¦205211 all¦205212 the Israeli¦205214 people from the Yehudah¦205215 and¦205216 Benyamin¦205216 tribes:
\v 4 Yahweh¦205221 says¦205220 that you¦205224 mustn't go¦205224 and¦205225 fight¦205227 with¦205228 your¦205230 relatives. Everyone¦205232 should just go home¦205233 again, because¦205234 everything that's happened¦205236 came from¦205235 me¦205235.” \add ≈So¦205239\add* they¦205239 listened¦205239 to the¦205242 \add #message¦205242\add* from Yahweh¦205243, and¦205244 \add ≈called off the planned attack\add* against¦205246 Yarov'am¦205248 \add !(Jeroboam¦205248)\add*.
\s1 Rehav'am fortifies the cities
\rem /s1 Rehoboam Fortifies Judah; Rehoboam Fortifies the Cities
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦205251\add* Rehav'am¦205252 \add !(Rehoboam¦205252)\add* lived¦205251 in¦205253 Yerushalem¦205253 \add !(Jerusalem¦205253)\add* and¦205254 \add ≈fortified¦205256\add* the cities¦205255 throughout Yehudah¦205257 \add !(Judah¦205257)\add*:
\v 6 Beyt¦205262-Lehem¦205264 \add !(Bethlehem¦205262)\add*, Eytam¦205267, Tekoa¦205270,
\v 7 Beyt¦205274-Tsur¦205276, Sokoh¦205279, Adulam¦205282,
\v 8 Gat, Mareshah¦205289, Zif¦205292,
\v 9 Adorayim¦205296, Lakish¦205299, Azekah¦205302,
\v 10 Tsor'ah¦205306, Ayalon¦205309, and¦205310 Hevron¦205312 (all in¦205314 Yehudah¦205314 and¦205315 Benyamin¦205315).
\v 11 He¦205319 strengthened¦205319 the¦205322 fortifications¦205322 \add in those cities and towns\add*, \add ≈appointed an army commander¦205325, and¦205326 stocked their storehouses¦205326 with\add* food¦205327 and¦205328 oil¦205328 and¦205329 wine¦205329.
\v 12 He \add also\add* \add ≈equipped each¦205331 of them with\add* shields¦205335 and¦205336 spears¦205336, and¦205337 \add ≈made¦205337 sure they were¦205340 well-protected\add*. \add ≈So\add* Yehudah¦205343 and¦205344 Benyamin¦205344 \add ≈were under his control\add*.
\s1 Priests and Levites go down to Yehudah
\rem /s1 Priests and Levites Support Rehoboam; Priests and Levites Come to Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 13 The¦205347 priests¦205347 and¦205348 Levites¦205348 throughout all¦205350 of Yisrael¦205352 \add !(Israel¦205352)\add* \add ≈supported¦205353 Rehav'am\add* \add !(Rehoboam)\add* \add ≈from¦205355 every¦205355 part of¦205357 the country¦205357\add*.
\v 14 The¦205362 Levites¦205362 abandoned¦205361 their¦205365 property¦205366 and their¦205366 pastureland¦205365 and¦205367 moved¦205367 to¦205369 Yerushalem¦205369 \add !(Jerusalem¦205369)\add* and across the rest of Yehudah¦205368 \add !(Judah¦205368)\add*, because¦205370 Yarov'am¦205373 \add !(Jeroboam¦205373)\add* and¦205374 his¦205374 sons¦205374 \add ≈stopped\add* them from¦205375 serving¦205375 as¦205375 Yahweh's¦205376 priests¦205375.
\v 15 \add ≈Instead\add* \add @Yarov'am¦205378\add* established¦205378 his own priests¦205381 for¦205382 his hilltop shrines¦205382 and¦205383 for¦205383 the goat and¦205384 calf¦205384 \add idols\add* that¦205385 he'd¦205386 made¦205386.\x + \xo 11:15: \xt 1Ki 12:31.\x*
\v 16 \add ≈As well as\add* \add @the¦205388 priests¦205388 and¦205388 Levites¦205388\add*, people from¦205389 all¦205389 the¦205390 Israeli tribes¦205390 \add ≈who¦205392 wanted to¦205396 serve\add* Yisrael's god Yahweh came¦205402 to Yerushalem¦205403 to¦205404 sacrifice¦205404 to¦205405 Yahweh¦205405, their¦205407 ancestors'¦205407 god.
\v 17 \add ≈So¦205409\add* they¦205409 strengthened¦205409 the¦205412 kingdom¦205412 of¦205412 Yehudah¦205413, and¦205414 as \add @the people\add* followed David's¦205426 and¦205427 Shelomoh's¦205427 \add !(Solomon¦205427)\add* examples, they strengthened Rehav'am's¦205417 \add rule\add* for¦205428 three years.
\s1 Rehav'am's family
\rem /s1 Rehoboam's Family; Rehoboam's Marriages
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 18 Rehav'am¦205434 \add !(Rehoboam¦205434)\add* \add ≈married\add* Mahalat¦205438. She was the¦205439 daughter¦205439 of¦205443 David's¦205445 son Yerimot¦205442, and her mother was Avihayil¦205446, the¦205447 daughter¦205447 of¦205447 Eliav¦205449 and \add ≈granddaughter\add* of¦205450 Yishay¦205452 \add !(Jesse¦205452)\add*.
\v 19 \add ≈They had\add* \add three\add* sons¦205456: Ye’ush¦205459, Shemaryah¦205462, and¦205463 Zaham¦205465.
\v 20 After¦205467 her¦205467, he¦205468 \add ≈married\add* Avshalom's¦205474 \add !(Absalom¦205474)\add* daughter¦205472 Ma’akah¦205471, and¦205475 they had \add four sons\add*: Aviyah¦205479, Atay¦205482, Ziza¦205485, and¦205486 Shelomit¦205488.
\v 21 Rehav'am¦205491 loved¦205490 Ma’akah¦205494 \add ≈the¦205495 most out of his eighteen wives¦205503 and¦205508 sixty¦205509 slave-wives\add*. He¦205510 fathered¦205510 twenty-eight sons¦205513 and¦205514 sixty¦205514 daughters¦205515,
\v 22 \add ≈but¦205517\add* \add *he\add* appointed¦205517 Ma’akah's¦205525 son¦205523 Aviyah¦205522 to¦205526 be the leader¦205526 of¦205527 his¦205527 \add older and younger\add* brothers¦205527, because¦205528 \add ≈that would mark him¦205529 as the future\add* king¦205529.
\v 23 He¦205531 wisely¦205531 sent his \add other\add* sons¦205535 to¦205536 \add ≈fortified¦205543\add* cities¦205542 across all¦205536 \add ≈the¦205538 regions\add* in Yehudah¦205539 \add !(Judah¦205539)\add* and¦205540 Benyamin¦205540, \add ≈where he¦205544 set them¦205545 up generously\add* and \add ≈asked the¦205546 local people¦205549 to¦205547 give¦205544 them wives¦205550\add*.
\c 12
\s1 Mitsrayim attacks Yehudah
\rem /s1 Egypt Invades Judah; Shishak Attacks Jerusalem; An Egyptian Invasion of Judah; Egypt Attacks Judah
\s4 Southern kingdom
\r (1 Kgs 14:25-28)
\p
\v 1 \add ≈However,\add* after Rehav'am¦205555 \add !(Rehoboam¦205555)\add* \add ≈had become established¦205553 and¦205556 in firm control of¦205556 his¦205556\add* kingdom¦205554, he¦205557 \add ≈and¦205562 all¦205562 the people\add* abandoned¦205557 Yahweh's¦205561 instructions¦205560.
\v 2 ⇔Because¦205581 they¦205582 were unfaithful¦205582 to Yahweh¦205583, King Shishak¦205574 from Mitsrayim¦205577 \add !(Egypt¦205577)\add* came¦205573 \add to attack\add* Yerushalem¦205580 \add !(Jerusalem¦205580)\add* in the¦205570 fifth¦205570 year¦205569 of Rehav'am's¦205572 \add reign\add*,
\v 3 with¦205585 1,200 chariots¦205587 and¦205588 sixty¦205588 thousand¦205589 horsemen¦205590, along with a huge number¦205592 of troops, including Mitsrim \add !(Egyptians)\add*, Luvim¦205599 \add !(Libyans¦205599)\add*, Sukim¦205600, and¦205601 Kushim.
\v 4 He¦205603 captured¦205603 Yehudah's¦205609 \add !(Judah¦205609)\add* \add ≈fortified¦205607\add* cities¦205606, then¦205610 moved towards Yerushalem¦205613.
\p
\v 5 Then¦205616 the¦205617 prophet¦205617 Shemayah¦205616 and¦205622 the¦205622 leaders¦205622 of¦205622 Yehudah¦205623 who'd¦205624 \add ≈fled\add* to¦205627 Yerushalem¦205629 because of¦205630 Shishak's¦205631 \add attacks\add* came¦205618 to¦205619 Rehav'am¦205621. \add @Shemayah¦205632\add* told¦205632 them¦205633, “Yahweh¦205637 says¦205636 that it was you \add people\add* who abandoned¦205639 me¦205640, \add ≈so¦205641\add* now I've¦205644 also¦205641 abandoned¦205644 you¦205645 \add ≈to be defeated by\add* Shishak¦205648.”
\p
\v 6 Then¦205654 the¦205654 king¦205654 and¦205650 the¦205651 Israeli¦205653 leaders¦205651 humbled¦205650 themselves¦205650 and¦205655 said¦205655, “Yahweh¦205658 \add ≈always does what's right¦205656 and fair\add*.”
\p
\v 7 When¦205660 Yahweh¦205661 saw¦205660 that¦205662 they'd¦205663 humbled¦205663 themselves¦205663, \add ≈he gave this\add* message¦205665 to¦205669 Shemayah¦205671, “They've¦205674 humbled¦205674 themselves¦205674, \add so\add* I¦205676 won't destroy¦205676 them¦205676—my¦205684 rage¦205684 won't pour¦205683 out¦205683 on¦205685 Yerushalem¦205685 \add ≈through¦205686 Shishak's¦205688 attack\add*, and I'll¦205677 give¦205677 them¦205678 \add ≈a¦205679 way to¦205680 recover\add* \add in the future\add*.
\v 8 \add ≈Nevertheless,\add* they'll¦205691 become¦205691 his servants¦205694, and¦205695 they'll¦205695 \add ≈learn¦205695\add* \add the difference between\add* \add ≈serving¦205696 me versus serving¦205697 other nations'¦205699 kings¦205698\add*.
\p
\v 9 \add ≈When¦205702\add* Mitsrayim's¦205706 \add !(Egypt¦205706)\add* King Shishak¦205703 \add ≈invaded\add* Yerushalem¦205709, he¦205710 took¦205710 the¦205713 treasures¦205713 from Yahweh's¦205716 \add ≈temple\add* and¦205717 the¦205721 king's¦205721 \add ≈palace\add*. He¦205725 took¦205725 everything¦205724 \add valuable\add*, \add ≈including¦205726\add* the¦205730 gold¦205730 shields¦205729 that¦205731 Shelomoh¦205733 \add !(Solomon¦205733)\add* had¦205732 made¦205732.\x + \xo 12:9: \xt 1Ki 10:16-17; 2Ch 9:15-16.\x*
\v 10 King¦205736 Rehav'am¦205737 \add ≈replaced them¦205738 with\add* bronze¦205740 shields¦205739, and¦205741 \add ≈distributed them¦205741 to the leaders of the people who¦205747 guarded¦205747\add* the¦205748 entrance¦205748 to the¦205750 king's¦205750 \add ≈palace¦205749\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈After that, whenever the¦205756 king¦205756 went¦205755 to Yahweh's¦205758 temple¦205757, the¦205760 guards went¦205759 with him carrying¦205761 those¦205761 bronze shields. Then when the king left again, they'd¦205762 return¦205762 them¦205762 to¦205763 the¦205765 guardroom¦205765\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Because\add* \add @Rehav'am¦205768\add* humbled¦205768 himself¦205768, Yahweh¦205773 \add ≈stopped¦205769 being angry¦205771 with him¦205770\add* and¦205774 didn't¦205774 \add ≈eliminate¦205775\add* him, \add ≈so¦205777\add* things¦205780 were¦205779 \add reasonably\add* good¦205781 in Yehudah¦205778 \add !(Judah¦205778)\add*.
