\v 1 In¦206909 the thirty-sixth year¦206909 of¦206913 \add King\add* Asa's¦206913 reign¦206912, Yisrael's¦206918 \add !(Israel¦206918)\add* king Baesha¦206915 \add ≈invaded\add* Yehudah¦206921 \add !(Judah¦206921)\add* and¦206922 built¦206922 Ramah¦206925 to¦206926 \add ≈prevent anyone¦206928 from leaving¦206928 or entering the¦206931 land controlled by\add* Yehudah's¦206932 King Asa.
\v 2 Asa¦206935 took¦206934 gold¦206937 and silver¦206936 from¦206938 the¦206938 \add ≈temple\add* treasuries¦206938 and¦206941 the¦206942 king's¦206942 \add ≈palace\add*, and¦206943 he¦206943 sent¦206943 \add it\add* to¦206944 King Ben¦206946-Hadad¦206948 of¦206949 Aram¦206950 \add !(Syria¦206950)\add* \add (modern Aram)\add*, who¦206951 lived¦206951 in¦206952 Damesek¦206952 \add !(Damascus¦206952)\add*, \add ≈requesting\add*,
\v 3 “\add I want\add* a¦206955 \add ≈peace treaty¦206955\add* between you¦206957 and¦206958 me, and¦206960 between¦206960 your¦206961 \add ≈family\add* and \add ≈mine\add*. Listen, I've¦206963 sent¦206963 gold¦206966 and silver¦206965 to you. Go¦206967 \add and\add* break¦206968 your¦206969 agreement with¦206970 Yisrael's¦206974 King¦206973 Baesha¦206972, \add ≈so¦206975\add* he'll¦206975 \add ≈give up¦206975 on¦206976 his attack\add* against me¦206976.”
\p
\v 4 Ben¦206979-Hadad¦206981 \add ≈accepted\add* King¦206984 Asa's¦206985 \add ≈suggestion\add* and¦206986 sent¦206986 his army¦206990 captains \add to fight\add* against¦206994 Yisrael's¦206997 cities. They¦206998 struck¦206998 Iyon¦207001, Dan¦207004, and¦207005 Avel¦207006-Mayim¦207007, and¦207008 all¦207009 the¦207011 storehouses¦207011 in the¦207012 Naftali¦207013 \add !(Naphtali¦207013)\add* cities.
\v 5 \add ≈When¦207015\add* \add King\add* Baesha¦207017 heard¦207016 \add about that\add*, he¦207018 stopped¦207018 \add ≈fortifying\add* Ramah¦207022 and¦207023 \add ≈abandoned the project\add*,
\v 6 \add ≈so¦207029\add* King¦207030 Asa¦207029 took¦207031 \add men there\add* from Yehudah¦207036. They¦207037 carried¦207037 away all¦207034 the¦207040 \add building\add* stones¦207040 from Ramah¦207041, along with the timber¦207044 which¦207045 Baesha¦207047 had¦207046 been using, and¦207048 used \add it all\add* to build¦207048 Geva¦207052 and¦207053 Mitspah¦207055 \add (north of Yerushalem\add* \add !(Jerusalem)\add* \add )\add*.
\s1 Hanani's prophecy about coming wars
\rem /s1 The Prophet Hanani
\s4 Southern kingdom
\p
\v 7 At¦207058 that¦207059 time¦207058, the¦207062 prophet¦207062 Hanani¦207061 went¦207060 to¦207063 Yehudah's¦207067 \add !(Judah¦207067)\add* King Asa¦207065 and¦207068 told¦207068 him¦207069, “Because¦207070 you¦207070 relied on¦207071 the¦207073 king¦207073 of¦207073 Aram¦207074 \add !(Syria¦207074)\add* \add ≈rather than\add* on¦207077 your¦207080 god¦207080 Yahweh¦207079, the¦207085 Aramean king's army¦207085 has¦207084 escaped¦207084 from¦207089 \add ≈being defeated by you\add*.
\v 8 Didn't¦207091 the¦207092 Kushim and¦207093 the¦207093 Luvim¦207093 \add !(Libyans¦207093)\add* \add ≈have a vast number¦207097 of\add* chariots¦207098 and¦207099 horsemen¦207099? Yet because¦207102 you¦207102 relied¦207102 on¦207103 Yahweh¦207105, he¦207106 \add ≈helped you defeat them¦207106\add*,
\v 9 because¦207109 Yahweh¦207110 \add ≈sees everything that's happening all¦207113 over the¦207115 world¦207115, and he strengthens¦207116 the people who¦207119 trust him¦207121 completely¦207120\add*. You've¦207122 been foolish¦207122 \add ≈in what you've just¦207125 done¦207122\add*, so from¦207127 now¦207127 on, you'll \add ≈be¦207128 facing\add* wars¦207130.”
\v 10 \add ≈But¦207132\add* \add King\add* Asa¦207133 was¦207132 angry¦207132 at the¦207136 prophet¦207136, very angry, and¦207137 had him put¦207137 in¦207142 \add ≈prison¦207139\add*, and¦207147 \add ≈after that¦207153\add* Asa¦207148 oppressed¦207147 some¦207149 of¦207149 \add &his¦207151\add* people¦207151.
