\p
\v 11 \add ≈All of¦207156 Asa's¦207157 projects from the¦207158 beginning of his reign to the¦207159 end\add* are¦207161 written¦207161 in the¦207164 scroll¦207164 about¦207164 the¦207165 kings¦207165 of¦207166 Yehudah¦207166 \add !(Judah¦207166)\add* and¦207167 Yisrael¦207167 \add !(Israel¦207167)\add*.
\v 12 \add King\add* Asa¦207170 \add ≈got¦207169 a disease that started in¦207171\add* his¦207174 feet¦207175 in¦207182 the thirty-ninth year¦207171 of¦207182 his¦207182 reign¦207174. \add ≈Even as it got worse,\add* he¦207185 didn't¦207183 \add ≈try¦207185 to get\add* Yahweh¦207188 \add to help him\add*, only doctors¦207190.
\v 13 Then¦207192 Asa¦207193 \add ≈died¦207197\add* in¦207198 the forty-first year¦207198 of¦207201 his¦207201 reign¦207201,
\v 14 and¦207203 he was buried¦207203 in¦207204 the tomb¦207204 that¦207205 \add ≈he'd¦207206 had¦207206 carved out\add* in¦207209 ‘The¦207209 City¦207209 of¦207209 David¦207210’. They¦207211 laid \add ≈his corpse on a bed of prepared¦207211 spices¦207215 and¦207216 perfumes¦207218 that had been mixed¦207217 ready\add*. Then¦207220 they¦207220 lit \add ≈a¦207223 large¦207224 bonfire\add* \add in his honour\add*.
