\v 1 Then¦207230 \add @Asa's\add* son¦207232 Yehoshafat¦207231 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦207231)\add* \add ≈replaced him¦207233 as king¦207230\add*, and¦207234 he¦207234 strengthened¦207234 \add ≈their defenses\add* against Yisrael¦207237 \add !(Israel¦207237)\add*.
\v 2 He¦207239 placed¦207239 \add ≈troops\add* in¦207242 all¦207242 of¦207244 Yehudah's¦207245 \add !(Judah¦207245)\add* fortified¦207246 cities, and¦207247 posted garrisons¦207248 across Yehudah¦207250 and¦207251 in¦207251 the¦207251 cities¦207251 in Efrayim¦207252 \add !(Ephraim¦207252)\add* that¦207253 his¦207256 father¦207256 Asa¦207255 had¦207254 captured¦207254.
\v 3 Yahweh¦207259 \add ≈helped\add* Yehoshafat¦207262 because¦207263 he¦207264 followed his¦207267 ancestor¦207267 David's¦207266 example at the¦207268 beginning, and¦207269 didn't¦207269 \add ≈ask the Baals¦207271 for guidance\add*,
\v 4 because¦207273 he \add ≈asked\add* his¦207275 father's¦207275 god, and¦207277 he¦207278 \add ≈followed God's instructions¦207277 rather than doing the¦207280 evil things that were done in\add* Yisrael¦207281.
\v 5 \add ≈So¦207283\add* Yahweh¦207284 \add ≈enabled him to maintain control of his\add* kingdom¦207287, and¦207289 all¦207290 of¦207290 Yehudah¦207292 brought tribute¦207293 to¦207294 Yehoshafat¦207294, \add ≈causing him to become very wealthy¦207298 and¦207300 highly respected¦207300\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈He was¦207303 completely devoted to doing what pleased\add* Yahweh¦207306, even removing¦207308 the¦207311 \add ≈hilltop¦207311 shrines¦207311\add* and¦207312 the¦207314 Asherah¦207314 \add poles\add* from¦207315 Yehudah¦207315.
\p
\v 7 In¦207318 the third year¦207318 of¦207318 his¦207320 reign¦207320 he¦207321 sent¦207321 his \add ≈officials¦207322\add*, Ben¦207323-Hayil¦207325, Ovadyah¦207326 \add !(Obadiah¦207326)\add*, Zekaryah¦207327 \add !(Zechariah¦207327)\add*, Netanel¦207328, and¦207329 Mikayah¦207329, to¦207330 teach¦207330 in¦207331 Yehudah's¦207332 cities¦207331.
\v 8 They were¦207334 accompanied by the¦207335 Levites¦207335 Shemayah¦207336, Netanyah¦207337, Zevadyah¦207338, Asahel¦207339, Shemiramot¦207340, Yonatan¦207342 \add !(Jonathan¦207342)\add*, Adoniyah¦207343, Toviyah¦207344, and Tov-Adoniyah, along with¦207348 two priests¦207351, Elishama¦207349 and¦207350 Yehoram¦207350 \add !(Jehoram¦207350)\add*.
\v 9 They¦207353 \add took\add* a scroll \add ≈with¦207355 Yahweh's¦207358 instructions¦207357 written on it\add*, and¦207359 went¦207359 around¦207359 Yehudah's¦207363 cities¦207362 teaching¦207364 the people¦207365.
\s1 Yehoshafat's rise
