\c 18
\s1 prophet Mikiyas and King Ahav
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat and Ahab; Micaiah Prophesies Against Ahab; Micaiah Predicts Failure; The Prophet Micaiah Warns Ahab
\s4 Both kingdoms
\r (1 Kgs 22:1-28)
\p
\v 1 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦207525 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦207525)\add* \add ≈became¦207529 very wealthy¦207526, and¦207527 was highly honoured¦207527\add*, \add ≈but then¦207529\add* he¦207529 allied himself by marriage to¦207530 \add Yisrael's\add* \add !(Israel)\add* \add King\add* Ahav¦207530.
\v 2 \add ≈Some years¦207534 later,\add* he went¦207550 \add ≈up¦207550\add* to Ahav¦207537 in Shomron¦207538 \add !(Samaria¦207538)\add*, and¦207539 Ahav¦207542 sacrificed lots of sheep¦207543 and¦207544 cattle¦207544 for him and¦207546 for¦207546 the people¦207546 who were with¦207548 him¦207548, and¦207549 he¦207549 incited¦207549 him¦207549 to \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207553-Gilead¦207554—
\v 3 Yisrael's¦207560 King Ahav¦207557 \add ≈suggested to¦207561\add* Yehudah's¦207565 \add !(Judah¦207565)\add* King Yehoshafat¦207563, “Will¦207566 you¦207566 \add ≈join\add* me¦207567 to \add attack\add* Ramot¦207568-Gilead¦207569?”
\p “\add ≈Wherever you'll be, I'll be there\add*,” he \add ≈responded\add*. “Your¦207574 people \add ≈are like my¦207575 own\add* people, and¦207576 \add we're\add* with¦207576 you¦207576 in¦207577 battle¦207577.”
\v 4 \add ≈Then¦207579 he¦207579 added\add*, “\add ≈But we should get Yahweh's¦207592 advice first\add*.”
\p
\v 5 \add ≈So¦207594\add* Yisrael's¦207597 king¦207595 gathered¦207594 four¦207601 hundred¦207602 \add of\add* \add &his¦207600\add* prophets¦207600 and¦207604 \add ≈asked¦207604\add* them¦207605, “Should we¦207606 \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207609-Gilead¦207610 or¦207612 not?”
\p “Go \add ≈ahead\add*,” they¦207615 answered¦207615, “and¦207617 God will¦207617 give¦207617 \add ≈victory to\add* the¦207620 king¦207620.”
\p
\v 6 \add ≈But¦207622\add* Yehoshafat¦207623 \add ≈asked¦207622\add*, “Is¦207624 there¦207624 no prophet¦207626 of Yahweh¦207627 here¦207625 that¦207629 we¦207629 can \add ≈ask¦207629\add*?”
\p
\v 7 Yisrael's¦207635 king¦207633 told¦207632 Yehoshafat¦207639, “\add There's\add* still¦207640 one¦207643 man¦207643 \add ≈who would ask\add* Yahweh¦207647, \add ≈but¦207649\add* personally I hate¦207650 him¦207650 because¦207651 \add ≈he¦207653 never prophesies¦207654 anything good¦207656\add* about¦207658 me—\add ≈it's always something\add* evil¦207661. He's¦207662 Yimla's¦207666 son¦207664, Mikayah¦207663.”
\p “\add ≈You shouldn't talk like that\add*,” said Yehoshafat.
\p
\v 8 \add ≈So¦207675\add* Yisrael's¦207677 king¦207676 \add ≈ordered¦207682\add* an official, “\add Get\add* Yimla's¦207688 son¦207686 Mikayah¦207684 \add here\add* \add ≈as quick¦207683 as possible\add*.”
\rem /s1 Micaiah Prophesies against Ahab
\p
\v 9 \add ≈Now\add* the¦207690 kings¦207690 of¦207690 Yisrael¦207691 and¦207692 Yehudah¦207695 \add !(Judah¦207695)\add* were¦207696 \add both\add* clothed¦207701 in \add &their\add* \add royal\add* robes¦207702 and sitting¦207696 there on¦207698 their \add #thrones¦207700\add* near Shomron's¦207707 \add !(Samaria¦207707)\add* entrance¦207705 gate¦207706. They were \add up\add* on a threshing¦207704 floor¦207704, and¦207708 all¦207708 the¦207710 prophets¦207710 were¦207711 prophesying¦207711 \add ≈in¦207712 front¦207712 of¦207712\add* them¦207712.
\v 10 Kena’anah's¦207719 son¦207717 Tsidkiyah¦207716 \add !(Zedekiah¦207716)\add* made¦207714 himself some iron¦207721 horns¦207720 and¦207723 said¦207723, “Yahweh¦207727 says¦207726 you'll¦207729 use these¦207728 to gore¦207729 Aram¦207732 \add !(Syria¦207732)\add* and destroy¦207735 them¦207735.”
\v 11 All¦207737 the¦207739 rest of Ahav's prophets¦207739 agreed, saying¦207742, “\add Yes,\add* go¦207743 and attack Ramot¦207744-Gilead¦207745 and¦207746 you'll succeed¦207746—Yahweh¦207748 will give¦207747 the¦207750 king¦207750 \add ≈victory\add*.”
\p
\v 12 The¦207752 messenger¦207752 who¦207753 went¦207755 to fetch Mikayah¦207758 \add ≈warned\add* him¦207760, “Listen, the¦207763 king¦207771 \add ≈is¦207772 pleased¦207774 with what the¦207764 other prophets¦207764 agreed on. Just say¦207761 the same as¦207776 them¦207777 and¦207778 give a¦207765 favourable message¦207775\add*.”
\p
\v 13 \add ≈But¦207781\add* Mikayah¦207782 \add ≈responded¦207781\add*, “As sure as Yahweh¦207785 lives¦207783, I'll¦207794 only say¦207791 what my¦207792 god¦207792 tells me to say¦207794.”
\p
\v 14 \add ≈When¦207796 he¦207796 got\add* to¦207797 the¦207799 king¦207799, King¦207801 \add Ahav\add* \add ≈asked¦207800\add* him¦207802, “Mikah¦207803, should we¦207804 \add ≈attack\add* Ramot¦207807-Gilead¦207808 for¦207809 battle¦207809, or¦207810 should I¦207812 \add ≈hold back\add*?”
\p “Go¦207814 \add ≈ahead\add* and¦207815 succeed¦207815,” he \add ≈answered\add*. “\add ≈You'll be¦207816 given¦207816 victory over them\add*.”
\p
\v 15 \add ≈But¦207819\add* the¦207821 king¦207821 said¦207819 to¦207820 him¦207820, “How¦207824 many¦207824 times¦207825 must¦207826 I¦207826 keep making¦207827 you¦207827 promise that¦207828 you'll¦207831 \add ≈only¦207833 say what Yahweh¦207837 says—not just what I want to hear\add*?”
\v 16 \add ≈So¦207839\add* \add @Mikayah¦207839\add* \add ≈responded¦207839\add*, “I¦207840 saw¦207840 all¦207843 of¦207843 Yisrael¦207845 \add !(Israel¦207845)\add* scattered¦207846 on¦207847 the¦207849 hills¦207849 like¦207850 sheep¦207850 without shepherds¦207855,\x + \xo 18:16: \xt Num 27:17; Eze 34:5; Mat 9:36; Mrk 6:34.\x* and¦207856 Yahweh¦207857 said¦207856, ‘\add ≈They don't¦207858 have any master¦207860, so they'll all just go home¦207865\add* in¦207866 peace¦207866.’ ”
\p
\v 17 \add ≈Ahav remarked\add* to¦207872 Yehoshafat¦207874 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦207874)\add*, “Didn't¦207875 I¦207876 tell¦207876 you¦207877 that he¦207880 wouldn't prophesy¦207880 anything good¦207882 about¦207869 me¦207881—only \add ≈disaster\add*?”
\p
\v 18 \add ≈But¦207889\add* \add @Mikayah¦207889\add* \add ≈continued¦207889\add*, “\add ≈Well, listen¦207891 to what Yahweh¦207894 says¦207889\add*. I¦207895 saw¦207895 Yahweh¦207898 sitting¦207899 on¦207900 his¦207902 throne¦207902, and¦207903 all¦207903 the¦207905 \add ≈heavenly¦207906 soldiers¦207905\add* standing¦207907 on¦207908 \add ≈each side of him\add*,
\v 19 and¦207913 Yahweh¦207914 said¦207913, ‘Who'll¦207915 entice¦207916 Yisrael's¦207922 King¦207920 Ahav¦207919 so¦207923 he'll¦207923 \add ≈attack\add* and¦207924 then \add ≈die\add* at¦207925 Ramot¦207925-Gilead?’ \add ≈Some suggested one thing, and others suggested something else\add*.
\v 20 Then¦207935 \add ?≈a\add* spirit¦207936 went¦207935 out¦207935 and¦207937 stood¦207937 \add ≈in¦207938 front¦207938 of¦207938\add* Yahweh¦207939 and¦207940 said¦207940, ‘I myself will¦207942 entice¦207942 him¦207942.’ ‘\add ≈How¦207946 would you do it\add*?’ Yahweh¦207944 \add ≈asked¦207943\add* him¦207945.
\v 21 \add @The¦207948 spirit¦207948\add* \add ≈replied¦207948\add*, ‘I'll¦207949 go¦207949 and¦207950 \add ≈inspire all¦207954 of¦207954 Ahav's prophets¦207956 to tell lies\add*.’ \add @Yahweh\add* said¦207957, ‘\add ≈That'll work\add*. Go¦207962 and¦207963 do¦207963 it.’
\p
\v 22 “\add ≈So¦207967\add* now¦207967, listen. Yahweh¦207970 placed¦207969 a¦207971 deceiving spirit¦207971 in¦207973 the¦207973 \add #mouths¦207973\add* of¦207973 those¦207975 prophets¦207974 of¦207974 yours, and¦207976 Yahweh¦207976 \add ≈has¦207977 decreed that you'll¦207978 face\add* disaster¦207979.”
\p
\v 23 Then¦207982 Kena’anah's¦207986 son¦207984 Tsidkiyah¦207983 \add !(Zedekiah¦207983)\add* \add ≈went up to\add* Mikayah¦207990 \add ≈and¦207987 slapped¦207987 him hard\add* on¦207991 the¦207993 cheek¦207993, saying¦207994, “\add Yeah?\add* \add ≈Since when did Yahweh's¦208001 spirit¦207999 leave¦207998 me¦208002 and start speaking¦208003 to¦208003\add* you¦208004?”
\p
\v 24 “Well, you'll \add ≈find out\add* \add soon\add*,” answered¦208006 Mikayah¦208007, “on the¦208010 day¦208010 when¦208012 you¦208013 go¦208013 room¦208014 by room¦208015 \add in some house\add* to \add ≈try to hide¦208016\add*.”
\p
\v 25 “\add ≈Arrest\add* Mikayah¦208024,” \add ≈ordered¦208018 King Ahav\add*, “and¦208025 return¦208025 him¦208025 to¦208026 Amon¦208028 the city¦208031 \add ≈governor\add*, and¦208032 to¦208032 \add ≈my\add* son¦208035 Yoash¦208034.
\v 26 \add ≈Tell¦208039 them that the¦208042 king's¦208042 ordered that this¦208044 man be put¦208043 in prison¦208046, and¦208047 be given only strictly-rationed bread¦208048 and¦208050 water¦208050 until¦208052 I return¦208053 safely\add*.”
\p
\v 27 “If¦208058 you¦208061 return¦208061 \add ≈safely\add*,” Mikayah¦208057 \add ≈retorted\add*, “then Yahweh¦208066 mustn't have¦208065 spoken¦208065 to me¦208067.”
