\p
\v 1 \add ≈Sometime after¦208439 that,\add* the¦208443 Moavim and¦208446 Amonim¦208450, along with¦208448 some¦208450 of¦208450 the¦208450 Meunim,\f + \fr 20:1 \ft Following the Septuagint for this.\f* came¦208442 to battle¦208454 against \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208453 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦208453)\add*.
\v 2 \add Some men\add* came¦208456 and¦208457 told¦208457 Yehoshafat¦208458, “A¦208462 \add ≈huge¦208463 army\add* is¦208460 coming¦208460 from¦208464 Aram¦208466 \add !(Syria¦208466)\add* beyond the¦208464 \add Dead\add* Sea¦208465 to attack you, and¦208467 take note: they're¦208467 \add already\add* in¦208468 Hatsatson-Tamar¦208469, also known as Eyn¦208471-Gedi¦208472.”
\v 3 Yehoshafat¦208476 \add ≈was¦208474 alarmed and¦208475 decided to¦208480 request¦208480 advice from\add* Yahweh¦208481, and¦208482 he¦208482 \add ≈ordered that all¦208487 of¦208487 Yehudah¦208489\add* \add !(Judah¦208489)\add* \add ≈should fast¦208484\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈So¦208491\add* Yehudah¦208492 assembled¦208491 to¦208493 \add ≈request¦208493 Yahweh's¦208494 help\add*—they¦208500 came¦208500 to Yerushalem \add !(Jerusalem)\add* from¦208496 all¦208496 of¦208498 Yehudah's¦208499 cities¦208498 to¦208501 \add ≈ask Yahweh¦208504 for help\add*.
\rem /s1 Jehoshaphat's Prayer and Victory
\p
\v 5 Yehoshafat¦208507 stood¦208506 in¦208508 front of all the people from Yerushalem¦208510 and across Yehudah¦208509, in¦208513 front¦208513 of¦208513 the¦208515 new¦208515 temple¦208511 courtyard¦208514,
\v 6 and¦208517 \add ≈prayed\add*, “Yahweh¦208518, the¦208519 god¦208519 of¦208519 our¦208520 ancestors¦208520, aren't¦208521 you¦208522 the god¦208525 \add who lives\add* in¦208526 the heavens¦208526? And¦208527 you¦208527 rule¦208528 in all¦208529 the¦208530 kingdoms¦208530 \add ≈around the¦208531 world\add*, and¦208532 \add ≈you have full power¦208533 and control\add*—no one can stand against you¦208536.
\v 7 Weren't you¦208541 our¦208542 god¦208542 who drove¦208543 the¦208546 previous inhabitants¦208546 of¦208546 this¦208548 land¦208547 out ahead of¦208550 your¦208550 Israeli¦208551 people¦208550? Didn't¦208539 you¦208552 give¦208552 it¦208552 to¦208553 the¦208553 descendants¦208553 of¦208553 Avraham¦208554—the one you loved forever¦208556?\x + \xo 20:7: \xt Isa 41:8; Jam 2:23.\x*
\v 8 \add @Our¦208558 ancestors¦208558\add* lived¦208558 in¦208560 \add @this¦208560 land¦208560\add* and¦208561 built¦208561 a¦208565 \add ≈temple to¦208567 honour you\add*, saying¦208567,
\v 9 ‘If¦208569 disaster¦208573, \add like\add* \add ≈war\add*, judgement¦208575, epidemic, or famine¦208577 comes¦208571 on¦208572 us¦208572, we'll¦208578 stand¦208578 \add ≈in¦208579 front¦208579 of¦208579\add* this¦208582 \add ≈temple\add*, and¦208583 \add ≈in¦208583 front¦208583 of¦208583\add* you¦208583, because¦208584 your¦208585 name¦208585 is¦208586 \add ≈honoured here\add*. And¦208588 we'll¦208588 cry¦208588 to¦208589 you¦208589 because of¦208590 our¦208590 distress¦208590, and¦208591 you'll¦208591 hear¦208591 and¦208592 rescue¦208592 us.’
\p
\v 10 You¦208606 didn't allow¦208606 our Israeli¦208607 ancestors to enter the¦208596 countries¦208611 of¦208596 Amon¦208598, Moav¦208599 \add !(Moab¦208599)\add*, or Edom when¦208610 they¦208610 were travelling from Mitsrayim¦208612 \add !(Egypt¦208612)\add* \add to Kena'an\add* \add !(Canaan)\add*. So our ancestors turned¦208614 away from¦208615 those¦208615 areas and¦208616 didn't¦208616 destroy¦208617 them¦208617,\x + \xo 20:10: \xt Deu 2:4-19.\x* but now¦208594 \add they're coming here to attack us\add*.
\v 11 Look¦208619 how they're¦208621 repaying¦208622 us¦208623 \add for not destroying them\add*—they come¦208624 \add here\add* to¦208625 drive¦208625 us¦208625 out¦208625 from¦208626 the \add ≈land\add* you¦208628 gave us¦208628 as an \add ≈inheritance¦208628\add*.
\v 12 \add So,\add* our¦208630 god¦208630, \add ≈please punish\add* them¦208634, because¦208635 \add ≈we're not¦208636 strong¦208638 enough to¦208639 battle this¦208642 huge¦208641 army that's¦208643 on¦208644 its way\add*. \add ≈We simply don't¦208646 know¦208647 what¦208648 to do¦208650, so¦208645 we're looking to you¦208652 to rescue us\add*.”
\p
\v 13 \add At that time,\add* all¦208655 of Yehudah¦208657 \add !(Judah¦208657)\add* (men, women¦208664, and¦208665 children¦208665) were¦208658 standing¦208658 \add ≈in¦208659 front¦208659 of¦208659\add* Yahweh¦208660,
\v 14 and¦208668 Yahweh's¦208689 spirit¦208688 came on Yahaziel. (Yahaziel was the¦208669 son¦208669 of¦208669 Zekaryah¦208671 \add !(Zechariah¦208671)\add*, son¦208672 of¦208672 Benayah¦208674, son¦208675 of¦208675 Yeiel¦208677, son¦208678 of¦208678 Matanyah¦208680 the¦208681 Levite¦208681, and a \add #descendant¦208684\add* of¦208684 Asaf¦208685.) In¦208690 the¦208690 middle¦208690 of¦208691 the¦208691 assembly¦208691
\v 15 he¦208693 said¦208693, “\add ≈Pay¦208694\add* attention¦208694, all¦208695 of¦208695 Yehudah¦208697, inhabitants¦208698 of¦208698 Yerushalem¦208699, and¦208700 King¦208700 Yehoshafat¦208701. Yahweh¦208705 has this to say¦208704 to¦208706 you all, ‘Don't¦208708 be¦208710 afraid¦208710, and¦208711 don't¦208711 be¦208713 dismayed¦208713 by this¦208717 \add ≈huge¦208716 force\add*, because¦208718 it's not¦208719 your battle¦208721, but God's¦208723.\x + \xo 20:15-17: \xt Deu 20:1-4.\x*
\v 16 Tomorrow¦208725, go¦208726 down¦208726 against them¦208727. Listen, they're¦208728 coming¦208729 uphill near the¦208730 Ascent¦208730 of¦208730 Tsits, and¦208732 you'll¦208732 find¦208732 them¦208733 at¦208734 the¦208734 end¦208734 of¦208734 the¦208735 valley¦208735, facing¦208736 the¦208737 Yeruel¦208738 wilderness¦208737.
\v 17 You¦208741 won't \add need\add* to¦208742 fight¦208742 \add ≈them—just¦208743 take¦208744 your¦208744 positions, people from Yerushalem¦208753 and wider Yehudah¦208752, and watch¦208746 Yahweh¦208750 save you¦208751\add*.\x + \xo 20:17: \xt Exo 14:13-14.\x* Don't¦208754 \add ≈be¦208756 afraid¦208756 or discouraged¦208759\add*. Go¦208761 out¦208761 \add ≈there\add* tomorrow¦208760 and¦208763 Yahweh¦208763 will¦208764 be¦208764 with¦208764 you¦208764.’ ”
\p
\v 18 Then¦208766 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208767 \add !(Jehoshaphat¦208767)\add* bowed¦208766 with \add &his\add* face¦208768 to¦208769 the¦208769 ground¦208769, and¦208770 all¦208770 \add the people from\add* Yerushalem¦208774 \add !(Jerusalem¦208774)\add* and across Yehudah¦208772 fell¦208775 \add to their knees\add* in¦208776 front¦208776 of¦208776 Yahweh¦208777 to¦208778 worship¦208778 \add *him¦208779\add*.
\v 19 Then¦208781 \add some of\add* the¦208782 Levites¦208782 who were descendants¦208785 of¦208785 Kohat and¦208787 Korah stood¦208781 up to¦208791 \add ≈loudly\add* praise¦208791 Yisrael's¦208794 \add !(Israel¦208794)\add* god¦208793 Yahweh¦208792.
\p
\v 20 They¦208799 rose¦208799 early¦208799 the \add next\add* morning¦208800 and¦208801 went¦208801 out¦208801 to¦208802 the¦208802 Tekoa¦208803 wilderness¦208802, and¦208804 \add ≈as they¦208804 were leaving\add*, Yehoshafat¦208806 stood¦208805 and¦208807 \add ≈called out\add*, “Hear¦208808 me¦208808, inhabitants¦208810 of¦208810 Yerushalem¦208811 and Yehudah¦208809. Believe in¦208813 \add ≈our\add* god¦208814 Yahweh¦208813, and¦208815 be¦208815 \add ≈confident\add*. Believe his¦208817 prophets¦208817 and¦208818 succeed¦208818.”
\v 21 Then¦208820 he¦208820 consulted¦208820 with the¦208823 people¦208823, and¦208824 he¦208824 appointed¦208824 some to sing¦208825 to¦208826 Yahweh¦208826 and¦208827 some to¦208828 praise¦208827 \add ≈him for his splendour¦208828 and sinlessness\add* as they went¦208831 out¦208831 in¦208832 front¦208832 of¦208832 the¦208833 \add enemy\add* army, and¦208834 they¦208834 were¦208834 saying¦208834, “Give¦208835 thanks¦208835 to¦208836 Yahweh¦208836, because¦208837 his loyal¦208839 commitment¦208839 \add endures\add* forever¦208838.”
\p
\v 22 As they¦208842 began¦208842 to sing and¦208844 praise¦208844 Yahweh¦208846, he¦208845 sent ambushers¦208848 against the¦208851 \add ≈Amonim, Moavim, and¦208854 Edomim\add* who¦208857 were attacking Yehudah¦208858, and¦208859 they¦208859 were¦208859 defeated¦208859.
\v 23 Then¦208861 the¦208862 \add ≈Amonim and¦208864 Moavim turned on¦208865 the Edomim and¦208872 completely¦208871 annihilated them¦208872\add*, and¦208873 \add ≈after that\add* they \add ≈slaughtered each¦208877 other\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈When¦208882 Yehudah's¦208882 men arrived¦208883 at the place overlooking the wilderness¦208887, wow, they saw corpses¦208893 all over the ground¦208895\add*. No one had escaped¦208897.
\p
\v 25 Then¦208899 Yehoshafat¦208900 and¦208901 his¦208901 people¦208901 went¦208899 to¦208902 plunder¦208902 the spoils, and¦208906 they¦208906 found¦208906 lots of goods among¦208907 them¦208907, as well as clothing,\f + \fr 20:25 \ft The Hebrew ‘bodies/corpses’ seems wrong here.\f* and valuable items¦208911. They¦208913 took that for¦208914 themselves \add ≈until there¦208915 was¦208915 nothing left to\add* carry¦208916 away—there was¦208925 \add ≈so much¦208925 plunder that it took three¦208919 days¦208918 to collect it¦208927 all\add*.
\v 26 On¦208929 the¦208930 fourth¦208930 day, they¦208931 assembled¦208931 in Berakah¦208933 Valley and praised Yahweh¦208940 there¦208936. That's¦208949 why it's called¦208944 Berakah¦208951 Valley \add (which means ‘praise/blessing’)\add* to this day¦208954.
\v 27 Then¦208956 all¦208957 the¦208959 \add #men¦208959\add* from Yerushalem¦208961 and¦208962 \add across\add* Yehudah¦208960 returned¦208964 to¦208965 Yerushalem¦208967 with¦208968 \add King\add* Yehoshafat¦208962 \add ≈leading¦208963 them\add*—celebrating because¦208969 Yahweh¦208972 had¦208971 enabled them¦208971 to defeat their¦208973 enemies¦208973.
\v 28 \add ≈When¦208975\add* they¦208975 arrived¦208975 at Yerushalem¦208976, they went¦208975 to¦208980 the¦208982 \add ≈temple¦208982\add*, \add playing\add* harps¦208978, lutes, and¦208979 trumpets¦208979.
\v 29 The¦208986 \add nearby\add* kingdoms¦208991 \add ≈were¦208985 all¦208989 very afraid of\add* God¦208987 when¦208993 they heard¦208993 that¦208994 Yahweh¦208996 had¦208995 fought¦208995 against Yisrael's¦208999 \add !(Israel¦208999)\add* enemies¦208998,
\v 30 \add ≈so¦209001\add* Yehoshafat's¦209003 kingdom¦209002 was¦209001 untroubled, and¦209004 his¦209006 god¦209006 gave¦209004 him \add ≈peace¦209001 from¦209007 all his neighbours\add*.
