\p
\v 21 King Uziyah¦211853 had¦211855 leprosy¦211855 until¦211857 he \add ≈died¦211860\add*, \add ≈so¦211861\add* he¦211861 had to live¦211861 in an isolated residence and wasn't allowed to \add ≈approach the temple\add*. His¦211871 son¦211871 Yotam¦211870 \add !(Jotham¦211870)\add* \add ≈stood in for him\add*—supervising the¦211874 \add ≈palace¦211874\add* and \add ≈ruling Yehudah\add* \add !(Judah)\add*.
