\v 9 \add ≈Now\add* there¦212237 was¦212238 a¦212239 prophet¦212239 of Yahweh¦212240 \add ≈named¦212242\add* Oded¦212241, and¦212243 he¦212243 went¦212243 out¦212243 to¦212244 \add &Yisrael's¦212245\add* \add !(Israel¦212245)\add* army¦212245 as it was¦212246 returning to¦212247 Shomron¦212247 \add !(Samaria¦212247)\add*, and¦212248 told¦212248 them¦212249, “Listen, your¦212255 ancestors'¦212255 god, Yahweh, \add ≈was angry\add* with Yehudah¦212258 \add !(Judah¦212258)\add*, so he¦212259 \add ≈helped you defeat them¦212259\add*. \add ≈However,\add* you¦212261 \add people\add* killed¦212261 them¦212263 in¦212264 rage¦212264, \add and\add* \add ≈God has¦212267 taken notice\add*.
