\v 22 During¦217064 the first year¦217064 that King¦217066 Koresh¦217066 \add !(Cyrus¦217066)\add* reigned over Paras¦217068 \add !(Persia¦217068)\add*, in order to¦217069 \add further\add* fulfil¦217069 what Yahweh¦217072 had said¦217093 via \add the prophet\add* Yirmiyah¦217074 \add !(Jeremiah¦217074)\add*, Yahweh¦217076 \add ≈worked on\add* the¦217079 spirit¦217079 of¦217079 King Koresh¦217080 who then¦217084 wrote¦217092 this ruling \add and sent messengers\add* to¦217084 announce it throughout his¦217089 kingdom¦217089:
\v 23 “I, Paras's¦217102 King¦217101 Koresh¦217099, declare that Yahweh¦217109, the¦217110 god¦217110 of¦217110 the¦217111 heavens¦217111, has given me all these earthly¦217106 kingdoms¦217105, and¦217112 he's given me¦217115 the job of building¦217116 a¦217119 house¦217119 for him in¦217120 Yerushalem¦217120 \add !(Jerusalem¦217120)\add*, which¦217121 is¦217122 in¦217122 Yehudah¦217122 \add !(Judah¦217122)\add*.\x + \xo 36:23: \xt Isa 44:28.\x* \add To help with that,\add* \add ≈anyone who's¦217123 from¦217126 there is allowed¦217132 to return¦217132, and may their god Yahweh¦217129 be with¦217131 them and help them\add*.
